    Question: Harper drinks a 1/2 bottle of mineral water per day. She buys the mineral water by the case at a big box store. They come 24 bottles to a case and are currently on sale for $12.00. If she wants to buy enough cases to last her 240 days, how much will she spend? Think step by step. Answer:Harper drinks a 1/2 bottle of mineral water per day, so she drinks 1/2 x 24 = 12 bottles per day. If she wants to buy enough cases to last her 240 days, she needs to buy 12 bottles per day x 240 days = 2880 bottles. Since there are 24 bottles per case, Harper will need to buy 2880 bottles / 24 bottles per case = 120 cases. Since each case costs $12, Harper will spend 120 cases x $12 per case = $1440. #### 1440 The answer is: 1440

